<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Memento Pattern" id="memento">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1434" dy="844" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="1200">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        
        <!-- Title -->
        <mxCell id="title" value="MEMENTO DESIGN PATTERN - Save &amp; Restore Object State (Undo Functionality)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1520" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- PURPOSE -->
        <mxCell id="purpose_title" value="PURPOSE: Capture &amp; externalize object's internal state WITHOUT violating encapsulation" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="70" width="1520" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- USE CASE -->
        <mxCell id="usecase_title" value="WHEN TO USE: Build UNDO/REDO functionality (snapshot + restore)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="120" width="1520" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- COMPONENTS -->
        <mxCell id="components_title" value="THREE KEY COMPONENTS" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="170" width="1520" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="components" value="1. ORIGINATOR (object whose state we want to save)&#xa;   - Represents object for which state needs to be saved &amp; restored&#xa;   - Creates Memento (snapshot of current state)&#xa;   - Restores state from Memento&#xa;   - KNOWS what to save &amp; how to restore (encapsulation preserved!)&#xa;   &#xa;2. MEMENTO (snapshot object that holds Originator's state)&#xa;   - Stores internal state of Originator&#xa;   - Immutable! (state fixed at creation time)&#xa;   - NO business logic (just data container)&#xa;   - Can store: full state or partial state (as needed)&#xa;   &#xa;3. CARETAKER (manages history of Mementos)&#xa;   - Maintains list of Mementos (history stack)&#xa;   - Provides: save() — add Memento to history&#xa;   - Provides: undo() — retrieve last Memento, remove from history&#xa;   - NEVER examines Memento contents (black box!)&#xa;   - NEVER modifies Memento (read-only access)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="210" width="1520" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- CODE EXAMPLE -->
        <mxCell id="code_title" value="CODE EXAMPLE: Configuration Manager with Undo" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="570" width="1520" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="code_example" value="// ORIGINATOR (Configuration — object to save/restore)&#xa;class Configuration {&#xa;  private int height;  // State to save&#xa;  private int width;   // State to save&#xa;  &#xa;  public Configuration(int height, int width) {&#xa;    this.height = height;&#xa;    this.width = width;&#xa;  }&#xa;  &#xa;  // ORIGINATOR knows what to save&#xa;  public ConfigurationMemento createMemento() {&#xa;    return new ConfigurationMemento(height, width);  // Snapshot!&#xa;  }&#xa;  &#xa;  // ORIGINATOR knows how to restore&#xa;  public void restore(ConfigurationMemento memento) {&#xa;    this.height = memento.getHeight();  // Restore from snapshot&#xa;    this.width = memento.getWidth();&#xa;  }&#xa;  &#xa;  // Change state&#xa;  public void setHeight(int h) { this.height = h; }&#xa;  public void setWidth(int w) { this.width = w; }&#xa;  &#xa;  public String toString() {&#xa;    return 'Config[' + height + ' x ' + width + ']';&#xa;  }&#xa;}&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;// MEMENTO (Snapshot of Configuration state)&#xa;class ConfigurationMemento {&#xa;  private final int height;  // Immutable!&#xa;  private final int width;   // Immutable!&#xa;  &#xa;  public ConfigurationMemento(int height, int width) {&#xa;    this.height = height;&#xa;    this.width = width;&#xa;  }&#xa;  &#xa;  // Getters only (no setters — immutable!)&#xa;  public int getHeight() { return height; }&#xa;  public int getWidth() { return width; }&#xa;}&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;// CARETAKER (Manages history of snapshots)&#xa;class ConfigurationCaretaker {&#xa;  private List&lt;ConfigurationMemento&gt; history = new ArrayList&lt;&gt;();&#xa;  &#xa;  // Save snapshot to history&#xa;  public void addMemento(ConfigurationMemento memento) {&#xa;    history.add(memento);&#xa;  }&#xa;  &#xa;  // Undo: Get last snapshot &amp; remove from history&#xa;  public ConfigurationMemento undo() {&#xa;    if (history.isEmpty()) return null;&#xa;    int lastIndex = history.size() - 1;&#xa;    ConfigurationMemento memento = history.get(lastIndex);&#xa;    history.remove(lastIndex);  // Remove from history&#xa;    return memento;&#xa;  }&#xa;}&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;// CLIENT (Uses Memento Pattern for undo)&#xa;class Client {&#xa;  public static void main(String[] args) {&#xa;    Configuration config = new Configuration(5, 10);&#xa;    ConfigurationCaretaker caretaker = new ConfigurationCaretaker();&#xa;    &#xa;    // Save initial state (snapshot 1)&#xa;    caretaker.addMemento(config.createMemento());&#xa;    System.out.println('Initial: ' + config);  // Config[5 x 10]&#xa;    &#xa;    // Change state&#xa;    config.setHeight(7);&#xa;    config.setWidth(12);&#xa;    &#xa;    // Save new state (snapshot 2)&#xa;    caretaker.addMemento(config.createMemento());&#xa;    System.out.println('After change: ' + config);  // Config[7 x 12]&#xa;    &#xa;    // Change state again&#xa;    config.setHeight(9);&#xa;    config.setWidth(14);&#xa;    System.out.println('After 2nd change: ' + config);  // Config[9 x 14]&#xa;    &#xa;    // UNDO! Restore to snapshot 2&#xa;    ConfigurationMemento memento = caretaker.undo();&#xa;    config.restore(memento);&#xa;    System.out.println('After undo: ' + config);  // Config[7 x 12]&#xa;    &#xa;    // UNDO again! Restore to snapshot 1&#xa;    memento = caretaker.undo();&#xa;    config.restore(memento);&#xa;    System.out.println('After 2nd undo: ' + config);  // Config[5 x 10]&#xa;  }&#xa;}&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;KEY POINTS:&#xa;  ✓ Configuration creates Memento (knows what to save)&#xa;  ✓ Configuration restores from Memento (knows how to restore)&#xa;  ✓ Caretaker stores Mementos (manages history)&#xa;  ✓ Caretaker NEVER examines Memento contents (encapsulation!)&#xa;  ✓ Client uses: save → change → undo (simple API)&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;BENEFITS:&#xa;  ✓ Undo/Redo functionality (time travel!)&#xa;  ✓ Encapsulation preserved (Originator decides what to save)&#xa;  ✓ Caretaker doesn't know Originator internals&#xa;  ✓ Multiple save points (history stack)&#xa;  ✓ Easy to implement versioning/snapshotting" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=9;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="610" width="1520" height="1180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- INTERVIEW QUESTIONS -->
        <mxCell id="q_title" value="INTERVIEW QUESTIONS" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1830" width="1520" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="questions" value="Q1: Memento vs Serialization for saving object state?&#xa;A1: MEMENTO: Selective state save (Originator decides what to save). In-memory snapshots. Fast (no I/O). Encapsulation preserved (Originator controls what's saved). SERIALIZATION: Full object graph saved. Disk/network I/O. Slower. Exposes all fields (reflection-based). Use Memento for in-memory undo/redo (text editor). Use Serialization for persistence (save to disk, database).&#xa;&#xa;Q2: Memory overhead of Memento Pattern?&#xa;A2: CONCERN: Each snapshot creates Memento object. Large object + many snapshots = memory hog! SOLUTIONS: (1) Incremental snapshots (save only changed fields, not full state), (2) Command Pattern + Memento (store commands, not full state), (3) Limit history size (keep last N snapshots), (4) Compress Mementos (serialize + compress), (5) Copy-on-write (share immutable data). Trade-off: memory vs undo depth.&#xa;&#xa;Q3: Memento Pattern in text editors (Ctrl+Z)?&#xa;A3: Text editors use MEMENTO! Example: VS Code, Word. Originator: Document (text content, cursor position). Memento: Snapshot of document state. Caretaker: UndoManager (history stack). On edit: save Memento. On Ctrl+Z: restore last Memento. Optimization: Don't save full document! Save diff (change delta) — insert/delete commands. Memento stores command, not full state. Efficient!&#xa;&#xa;Q4: How to implement REDO (not just UNDO)?&#xa;A4: TWO stacks! (1) Undo stack: stores past Mementos, (2) Redo stack: stores undone Mementos. UNDO: Pop from undo stack, push to redo stack, restore. REDO: Pop from redo stack, push to undo stack, restore. NEW EDIT: Clear redo stack (can't redo after new change). Example: undoStack=[M1, M2, M3], undo → undoStack=[M1, M2], redoStack=[M3]. Redo → undoStack=[M1, M2, M3], redoStack=[].&#xa;&#xa;Q5: Memento vs Command Pattern for undo?&#xa;A5: COMPLEMENTARY! MEMENTO: Saves STATE (snapshot). Good for: complex state, hard to reverse. COMMAND: Saves ACTIONS (commands with undo() method). Good for: reversible operations (insert text → delete text). HYBRID: Command Pattern for actions + Memento for state. Example: Text editor stores commands (insert, delete) but also periodic Mementos (checkpoints). Fast undo (commands) + safety net (Mementos). Best of both!" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=10;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1880" width="1520" height="480" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
